.TH BLIT.ENV 5 "2026-10-29" "Blit @VERSION@" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
blit.env \- startup environment of the Blit display server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/blit/blit.env
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I /etc/blit/blit.env
holds the environment that
.B blit.service
starts
.BR blit (8)
with.
It is read by
.BR systemd (1)
through
.BR EnvironmentFile= ,
not by Blit itself, so it follows systemd's rules: one
.IB NAME = value
per line, lines starting with
.B #
ignored, no shell expansion.
.PP
These are startup values.
Most of what an operator changes day to day \(em fonts, panes, the
compositor, frame timing, the login manager, pointer and keyboard
settings, the shutdown chord \(em is saved through the API in
.I /var/lib/blit/settings.json
and replaces the value given here.
Every variable is described in
.BR blit (8).
.PP
The file contains the API token, so it is mode 0640, owned by root and
group blit.
Restart the service after changing it:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo systemctl restart blit
.EE
.RE
.SH DEFAULT CONTENTS
The package creates the file on first installation and leaves it alone
afterwards:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
BLIT_BIND_ADDRESS=0.0.0.0
BLIT_DISPLAY_BACKEND=kms
BLIT_UPDATE_TOKEN_FILE=/etc/blit/update.token
BLIT_EXPECT_DESKTOP=1
BLIT_LOGIN_AUTOSTART=1
LANG=C.UTF-8
LC_ALL=C.UTF-8
BLIT_AUTH_TOKEN=\fIgenerated\fP
.EE
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Listen on the local machine only:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
BLIT_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
.EE
.RE
.PP
Let sessions run only a shell and Hibr:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
BLIT_COMMAND_ALLOWLIST=/bin/bash,/usr/bin/hibr
.EE
.RE
.PP
Start without the login manager, for a kiosk that starts its own session
through the API:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
BLIT_LOGIN_AUTOSTART=0
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/blit/blit.env
This file.
.TP
.I /etc/blit/update.token
The update token named by
.BR BLIT_UPDATE_TOKEN_FILE .
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/blit/examples/blit-unprivileged.conf
A
.BR systemd.unit (5)
drop-in that runs Blit as the unprivileged
.B blit
user.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR blit (8),
.BR blit-update-helper (8),
.BR systemd.exec (5)
